    "payload": {
      "content": "When evaluating Significance, prioritize the breadth of the problem addressed (SIGN-BRD) and the magnitude of improvement over state-of-the-art (SIGN-SOT). A key pitfall is accepting empirical analyses on simple, low-dimensional benchmarks (e.g., MNIST) as sufficient evidence for domain impact (SIGN-DOM); reviewers should demand validation on complex, real-world datasets to ensure generalizability. Distinguish between diagnostic observations of existing architectures and the proposal of new SOTA methods; the latter is required for high significance scores. Furthermore, assess real-world and societal impact (SIGN-IMP) by checking if the paper discusses practical deployment scenarios, safety-critical applications, or mitigation strategies for identified vulnerabilities, rather than just theoretical trade-offs.",
